{
  "$comment": [
    "One photograph for each generated playlist that has one, chosen once and shipped with the app.",
    "",
    "WHY IT IS PINNED AND NOT SEARCHED. The app does not fetch these covers. A fetch needs a Pexels",
    "key, and that key is not in this repository, so an install without it would have no photo",
    "covers at all. The choice is the id below; the query beside it records how the choice was found",
    "and is not re-run. Running the generator with the same ids fetches the same eighty-three",
    "photographs.",
    "",
    "WHERE THESE EIGHTY-THREE CAME FROM. They are photographs that were looked at and kept, each with",
    "the query it was found by. So the shipped set is a reviewed set, not a fresh search result that",
    "nobody has seen.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS NOT HERE. A list with no entry draws its figure from its own two numbers instead. The",
    "moods break out by genre and by decade, so there are more lists than entries, and some lists",
    "have no photograph. To add one, add an id and a query in this file.",
    "",
    "THE LICENCE. Every one of these is under the Pexels License: free to use, commercial included,",
    "no attribution required, and redistribution as part of a work is allowed, which is what shipping",
    "them in Assets is. What the licence forbids is not done here: the photographs are not resold",
    "unaltered, nothing implies a photographer endorses this, and nobody in them is shown in a bad",
    "light. The photographer is recorded anyway, in 'by' and 'page', because the credit costs one line",
    "and is fair to the photographer.",
    "",
    "NO FACES. No line in the app's own query table asks for a person, and every photograph here was",
    "additionally put past a face detector before it was kept. A picture added to this file by hand",
    "has had neither check run on it, so look at it first.",
    "",
    "SHAPE. A cover is a square and these are cut to it, centred, at the size the cover is composed",
    "at: 640. The app scales what it reads to fill the square, so a picture of any other shape still",
    "works and loses its edges. The mood's colour and the app's mark are NOT in these files; they go",
    "on at the moment the cover is drawn, from the list's own palette entry, so changing either",
    "reaches every one of these without a re-export.",
    "",
    "THE 'list' FIELD is the list's English name, for the credit line on the About screen and for",
    "reading this file. Nothing draws it. It is not localized and does not need to be: the About",
    "screen names each photograph's subject the same way the genre photographs name a shelf."
  ],
